  "question": {
    "text": "The number of bent-shaped molecule/s from the following is ______&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup><mfenced><mi>Azide</mi></mfenced><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>+</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>&#8596;</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#175;</mo></mover><mo>-</mo><mover><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>+</mo></mover><mo>&#8801;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math></p><p>It has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>sp</mi></math> hybridised central atom. Hence it is linear in shape.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">I</mi><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>(triiodide):</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/07cf062f-94fa-4871-88a9-3322b5a1cbdd.png\" style=\"width: 80px; height: 101px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>It has linear geometry, <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi></math> hybridisation with three lone pairs at central atom.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>NO</mi><mn>2</mn><mo>-</mo></msubsup></math>&nbsp;(nitrite) :&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/e5552e74-0bd0-4002-b290-4d2f1de5de55.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 103px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>It is (nonlinear) bent shaped as it has <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybridisation with one lone pair at central atom.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;(ozone) :&nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/a9706b58-2767-4790-9433-f375063942ef.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 108px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>It Is bent in shape with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math>&nbsp;hybridisation and one lone pair at central atom.</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>SO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>(sulphur dioxide) :&nbsp;</p><p>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/75838692-826d-4460-ab8c-4ce971f5f65f.png\" style=\"width: 120px; height: 108px;\" />&nbsp;</p><p>It is bent in shape with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>sp</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> hybridisation and one lone pair at central atom.</p><p>So&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>3</mn></math>&nbsp;among the given molecules is bent in shape.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
